Package: @alchemy.run/domain
Applies-to: vendor/alchemy/alchemy.run-domain-e1c3e6d.tgz
Upstream: not yet reported
Why: Verify runs each sequence its search found as a `Story`, and a `Story` starts its clock at a time of its own
  (2026-01-01 at this pin). The search gives the commands of a short sequence one time, the solver's first (the
  epoch), and a sequence whose commands share one time is written with no clock step. A `decide` that reads `now`
  (the usage model's allowance works out its day from it) then records another day when the sequence runs as a story
  than the search read, and Verify reports that the model does something else. With this every found sequence sets
  the clock before its first command, so the story runs it when the search did, whatever time the story starts at.
Remove-when: The library's found sequences set the clock the search used before their first command.
  `bun run beep patches prove` then says this patch's test passes without it.
Test: test/alchemy-domain/04-a-found-sequence-keeps-its-time/FoundSequenceTime.test.ts

